<title>USA: Belo says Columbia won't buy AHN.</title>
<headline>Belo says Columbia won't buy AHN.</headline>
<dateline>DALLAS 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>A.H. Belo Corp said on Wednesday that Columbia/HCA Health Care Corporation failed to close as scheduled last week on its purchase of Belo's interest in America's Health Network (AHN).</p>
<p>Belo and Columbia announced their initial agreement on May 13, 1997 for Belo to sell the 24-hour health news cable channel.</p>
<p>&quot;Belo's strategy regarding AHN is unchanged,&quot; Belo chairman, president and chief executive Robert Decherd said in a statement. &quot;We will explore our options and the company will not be funding AHN's operations.&quot;</p>
</text>
